{{>api_info}}

defmodule {{moduleName}}.ApiClient do
  @moduledoc """
  Behaviour for API HTTP transport.

  Implementations handle the actual HTTP request/response cycle and must define
  `send_request/5`. The default implementation is `#{inspect({{moduleName}}.DefaultApiClient)}`.

  An implementation that can hand out a response whose body has not been read
  yet also defines `send_streaming/6`, which the operations that return a
  `#{inspect({{moduleName}}.ByteStream)}` call. It is optional: an
  implementation written before streaming keeps working for every buffered
  call, and a streaming call on it fails with a `RuntimeError` that names it.

  Implementations may optionally accept a 6th `opts` keyword list via
  `send_request/6` to carry per-request transport hints. Currently recognised
  keys:

    * `:no_redirect` - when `true`, the implementation must NOT follow any 3xx
      redirect and instead returns the first 3xx response to the caller as-is
      (it does not raise). Used by the OAuth2 token endpoint POST so that a
      malicious or misconfigured server cannot replay the credentialed body to
      an attacker-controlled URL; the caller inspects and rejects the 3xx
      itself. Defaults to `false`.

    * `:no_default_headers` - when `true`, the implementation must not add the
      transport's default headers to the call. Used for token endpoints and
      OpenID Connect discovery, which live on another host than the API.
      Defaults to `false`.
  """

  @doc """
  Send an HTTP request and return the response.

  ## Parameters

    * `method` - HTTP method atom (e.g. `:get`, `:post`, `:put`, `:delete`).
    * `url` - Fully qualified URL string.
    * `headers` - Map of header names to values.
    * `body` - Request body (serialized JSON string, binary, map for multipart form data, a
      `#{inspect({{moduleName}}.BodySource)}` for a raw binary upload, or `nil`). Read a `BodySource`
      with `#{inspect({{moduleName}}.BodySource)}.open/1`; send it as it is read, with its length as
      `Content-Length` when that is known and chunked when it is not.

  ## Returns

    An `#{inspect({{moduleName}}.ApiHttpResponse)}` struct containing status code, body, and headers.
  """
  @callback send_request(
              client :: struct(),
              method :: atom(),
              url :: String.t(),
              headers :: %{optional(String.t()) => String.t()},
              body :: term() | nil
            ) :: {{moduleName}}.ApiHttpResponse.t()

  @doc """
  Send an HTTP request, optionally refusing to follow redirects.

  Variant of `send_request/5` that carries a per-request `opts` keyword list.
  When `:no_redirect` is `true`, any 3xx response (including 307/308) is
  returned to the caller as-is rather than being replayed to the `Location`
  target.

  The default behaviour delegates to `send_request/5` when no opts are set, so
  legacy clients without this callback remain valid behaviours; transport
  implementations that own the redirect loop should implement this callback and
  honour the flag.
  """
  @callback send_request(
              client :: struct(),
              method :: atom(),
              url :: String.t(),
              headers :: %{optional(String.t()) => String.t()},
              body :: term() | nil,
              opts :: keyword()
            ) :: {{moduleName}}.ApiHttpResponse.t()

  @doc """
  Releases any resources held by this client (connection pool, sockets).

  Implementations may be a no-op; implementations that own a pooled HTTP client
  should dispose of it. This is a no-op when the underlying HTTP library uses a
  globally supervised connection pool (as Req/Finch does).
  """
  @callback close(client :: struct()) :: :ok

  @doc """
  Send an HTTP request and return as soon as the response headers are accepted,
  with the body not read yet.

  The redirect, header and deadline rules are those of `send_request/6`, up to
  the headers. `opts` takes the same keys, and `:idle_timeout` (milliseconds, or
  `nil` for none) for the longest silence in the body; `:timeout` and
  `:deadline` stop at the headers. Retries and the 401 replay run in the caller
  of this callback, which never retries after the first body byte has been
  handed to the caller. A non-2xx response is returned like any other, with its
  body open.

  Returns an `#{inspect({{moduleName}}.ApiStreamResponse)}`: the status, the
  lower-cased headers, the body as an `Enumerable` of binaries (decoded when the
  server compressed it) and a zero-arity `close` function that aborts the
  connection instead of draining it. Reading the body raises
  `#{inspect({{moduleName}}.Errors.StreamError)}` when the connection fails after
  the headers and `#{inspect({{moduleName}}.Errors.NetworkTimeoutError)}` when it
  stays silent longer than `:idle_timeout`.
  """
  @callback send_streaming(
              client :: struct(),
              method :: atom(),
              url :: String.t(),
              headers :: %{optional(String.t()) => String.t()},
              body :: term() | nil,
              opts :: keyword()
            ) :: {{moduleName}}.ApiStreamResponse.t()

  @optional_callbacks close: 1, send_request: 6, send_streaming: 6
end
